# src/test.cyr — the `[build].test` hook, DELIBERATELY EMPTY.
#
# ⛔ DO NOT PUT A GATE HERE. `cyrius test` with no arguments auto-discovers `tests/*.tcyr` and does NOT
# run this file, so an assertion added here executes only when someone types `cyrius test src/test.cyr`
# by hand — i.e. never, and never in CI. crab's real suite lives in **`tests/crab.tcyr`**.
#
# This was found the expensive way: an `AE-6` precondition suite was written into this file, reported
# "2 passed" from the *other* file's placeholder asserts, and looked green. Same class as a CI that never
# builds a target — the gate existed and was not wired to anything.
fn main() { return 0; }

var r = main();
syscall(SYS_EXIT, r);
